Falsifies `socket_contract::verification::a_peer_word_round_trips_for_every_host_and_port`.

The defect: `peer_word` packs the address one bit too low, so it overlaps the port's top bit and the
word no longer reads back as the pair it was made from.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!` on `word_peer(word)`.

diff --git a/crates/socket_contract/src/lib.rs b/crates/socket_contract/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/socket_contract/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/socket_contract/src/lib.rs
@@ -135,7 +135,7 @@
 ///
 /// Name: provisional, minted 2026-11-11 (UTC) by lane/accept-reply-carries-the-peer.
 pub const fn peer_word(octets: [u8; 4], port: u16) -> u64 {
-    (u32::from_be_bytes(octets) as u64) << 16 | port as u64
+    (u32::from_be_bytes(octets) as u64) << 15 | port as u64
 }
 
 /// The peer a [`peer_word`] names, or `None` for the word 0 that a reply without a peer carries
